# A realistic rules file for `real-brokerage-preamble.xlsx`, once converted.
#
# It exists to prove one thing end to end: that the converted CSV is something
# REAL hledger reads. Before the trailer was trimmed this file produced
#
#     could not parse "" as a date using date format "%m/%d/%Y"
#     record: ,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
#
# and hledger abandoned the whole read — all 34 transactions — on that one
# record. The user reasonably concluded their rules file was broken. It was not,
# and this is that rules file.
#
# Driven by `crates/ledgeline-core/tests/convert_tabular.rs`, env-gated behind
# LEDGELINE_HLEDGER_CONVERT_CHECK, which converts the workbook, writes the CSV
# to a scratch directory and runs hledger over it.

skip 1

# All fifteen columns the export writes, in order. The ones with no meaning to
# hledger still have to be named, or `amount` would land on the wrong column.
fields date, txndate, statementaccount, institution, activity, checknumber, cardnumber, description, symbol, cusip, memo, tags, quantity, price, amount

date-format %m/%d/%Y
currency $

account1 assets:brokerage:cash
account2 expenses:unknown

if FEE
    account2 expenses:fees:bank

if DIVIDEND
    account2 income:dividends
